### 20 November 2026: checks completed; satisfaction confirmation pending

Read the README, repository context, agreed research question, evidence inventory and storyline. Issue 01 remains resolved; the agreed question, 30+/under-30 contrast and roles of H1/H2/H2b/volume are unchanged.

The user clarified: “The samples in H1 and H2 has no relation expect they both describe the premier league. they are not from the same source and that is a product of how we could aqquire data. For H1 - Keep existing samples and disclose limitations”. Recorded decision: describe separate study samples acquired through different routes; no shared recruitment-to-coverage cohort. Keep H1's sample, rules and results unchanged and disclose the verified limitations. No new sample restrictions or hypothesis analyses were implemented.

The [full comparison and evidence-status distinctions](../evidence_and_sources.md#issue-02-sample-and-provenance-audit-20-november-2026) are now recorded in evidence_and_sources.md. Supporting artifacts: [read-only audit script](issue02_sample_audit.py), [findings and input hashes](issue02_sample_audit.json), [event linkage](issue02_signing_linkage.csv).

| Verified dimension | H1 | Text |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Units and players | 19,712 events; 5,213 players | 1,332 selected signings; 980 players. Main sentiment: 820 signings; 613 players |
| Age groups | 18,398 under 30; 1,314 aged 30+ | Selected: 1,244 / 88; main: 753 / 67; H2b all-controls: 728 / 65 |
| Dates and seasons | 2001-01-01–2027-06-30; recorded labels 00/01–26/27, missing 01/02 | Signings 2012-07-01–2025-06-10; July–June season values 2012–2024. Articles 2011-07-22–2026-06-09 |
| Selection | Real-club origin outside PL under source season; upstream top-five endpoint and club-ID restrictions; no value/loan-return filter | PL destination under date-derived season, age 18–36, transfer-record market value >= EUR 2m, same-club/heuristic-return exclusions; PL/youth/non-club origins permitted |
| Age calculation | Completed years; observed 16–41 | Completed years; no disagreement on matched events |
| Text requirements | Not applicable | Main: no liveblogs/match reports, >=5 sentences in each before/after period. Volume uses all 1,332; H2b 793 follows quote removal and renewed threshold |
| Source status | Transfermarkt data and league lookup | Guardian content; Transfermarkt-derived signing metadata. Acquisition histories are separate, as clarified by the user |

**Checks passed:** reconstructing raw -> cleaned -> reduced -> H1 reproduces event membership exactly. Running the existing NLP selector with saving disabled reproduces every saved column for all 1,332 signings. Article metadata reproduces the saved before/after coverage counts; all four main-model per-signing ID sets agree. The provisional starting-context suggestion of different age calculations is superseded: the eligibility ranges and season conventions differ, but both calculate completed-years age.

**Matching check, for provenance only:** every selected text event occurs in local raw transfers. Matching player ID, transfer date and both club IDs finds 949 selected events (52 older) and 519 main events (37 older) in H1. Nonmatches comprise PL origins (330 selected / 276 main), graph club exclusions (50 / 23), and non-club origins (3 / 2); none is unexplained. These overlaps do not define a shared analytical cohort or common acquisition history. No matched-subset outcome analysis was performed or agreed.

**Disclosures to retain:**

- H1 includes 11 future-dated events, all under 30, including 3 PL arrivals. Its latest nonfuture date is 15 August 2026, and late-season coverage is partial; early coverage is sparse. Do not describe all events as completed moves or all labelled seasons as fully observed.
- H1's club list excludes senior clubs as well as youth/reserve sides; two selected text signings from Boca Juniors illustrate this. Its top-five endpoint restriction narrows the denominator beyond all transfers originating outside the PL.
- H1 retains 6,881 unpaid/missing-fee reversals under the text pipeline's 730-day heuristic. They are not confirmed loan-return labels. Text retains 74 paid reversals under its documented exception; it is not a permanent-transfer-only sample.
- Source-season and July–June conventions disagree for 283 H1 records and 7 text signings. Delap's June 2025 move changes origin league status between conventions. Retain existing conventions and state them.
- Repeated players occur in both analyses, and different signings can share articles. Neither is a unique-player cohort. Main H2's coverage threshold retains 67/88 older versus 753/1,244 younger signings.
- Documentation reports Guardian fetching on 4–7 November 2026 and a B5 rebuild on 8–9 November. Exact Kaggle version/download dates and cache completeness cannot be independently verified. The latest requested article date precedes the documented fetch, but full retrieval cannot be certified. The retired-player explanation for sparse histories remains a documentation claim.
- Article-link metadata is available locally, correcting the broader absence suggested by the older context. Raw article bodies, sentence text and model score caches are absent at the documented paths. H2b's saved table verifies 793, but the precise 27 exclusions from its 820-row base cannot be reconstructed locally.

**Completion review:** the verified population descriptions and explicit explanation of the relationship are written; the user has decided to retain the existing H1 sample. No further analysis is currently proposed. Original acquisition/version gaps and inaccessible text inputs are disclosed as limits. User satisfaction with this recorded description is still required before changing Status to Resolved. The README records this same handoff. After confirmation, proceed to issue 03 with the existing H1 definition; text measurement/results reviews remain in issues 04–05.

### Follow-up: common period proposed, not agreed

The user subsequently asked whether limiting H1 to 2012–2025 would strengthen the paper. No restriction or hypothesis rerun was authorised. Counts verified: recorded seasons 2012/13–2024/25 contain 16,636 events (15,573 under 30; 1,063 aged 30+) / 4,602 players; date interval 1 July 2012–30 June 2025 contains 16,652 events (15,585 / 1,067) / 4,607 players. See the [discussion and recommendation](../evidence_and_sources.md#follow-up-discussion-restricting-h1s-period).

Proposed recommendation: a main H1 using recorded seasons 2012/13–2024/25, with the original broad-period result retained as a sensitivity comparison. This improves historical scope and removes the sparsest early and partial/future late coverage, while retaining about 84% of events and 81% of older events. It does not create a common cohort or fix the other eligibility limits; H1 already shuffles within season. The effect on results is unknown and untested. This proposal supersedes the preceding statement that no further analysis is proposed, but does not supersede the user's retention decision unless the user agrees. Next action: discuss period definition and whether to authorise that rerun before seeking satisfaction confirmation or resolving issue 02.

### Follow-up: community input confirmed

The user asked whether community results use the same data as H1. Verified: current saved Louvain and Leiden both use all 19,712 events in `outsideprem_toprem_eligible_transfers.csv.gz`, exactly H1's main sample. The shared and both method-specific metadata hashes match the current input; independent aggregation exactly reproduces all 12,794 saved directed routes and weights (1,254 clubs). H1 removes zero rows from this prefiltered input. Communities aggregate across ages and seasons; H1 uses age-labelled events. They have different null models, and communities do not use H1's one-transfer-per-player sensitivity sample. See [full verification](../evidence_and_sources.md#follow-up-verification-community-results-use-the-same-h1-events).

Keeping a single transfer population after a period change would therefore require rerunning the community graph/null/partitions as well as H1. No rerun or period change has been implemented; the period decision remains under discussion and Issue 02 stays Open.

